INT. ORBITAL RECYCLING DEPOT - SORTING FLOOR - SHIFT CHANGE

Conveyor belts shuttle crushed satellites past a gantry. Sparks. The smell of hot solder.

KIRA ASANTE-VOLKOV (30s, sorter, welding mask pushed up) pulls a gray panel off the belt, turns it over. A strip of tape on the back: a name, scratched through.

Across the floor, DMITRI OLUWASEUN (50s, shift lead, clipboard) watches her. He does not look at the panel. He looks at her hands.

KIRA
This is from Sector Nine.

DMITRI
Everything's from Sector Nine.

KIRA
It's still warm.

He sets down the clipboard. Walks over. Slowly. The belt grinds.

DMITRI
Put it back.

KIRA
It has a serial.

DMITRI
Put it back on the belt.

She doesn't. A door hisses open at the far end. A third figure strides in: INSPECTOR LEOPOLDINE HARGROVE-SATO (40s, gray coat, a slim case). The belts slow, then stop. Silence.

LEOPOLDINE
Good morning. Please step away from the panel.

Kira lowers it. Dmitri straightens, pulls his clipboard to his chest.

LEOPOLDINE (CONT'D)
Which of you is Asante-Volkov?

Neither answers. The belt starts again, with a lurch.
